      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T02:52:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The LSB of the 4-byte code is be sent first in the PUT_IOWR_SHORT transaction.\nHence, it is also firstly put to DP80BUF and printed to the console.\nTake the following real AMD 4-byts Port 80 eSPI transaction for example:\n\"PUT_IOWR_SHORT(47),,,,0080,00 04 E2 EE,,87\"\nYou would like the Port code printed like this order \"EE E2 04 00\" instead of \"00 04 E2 EE\"\nIs it correct?",
      "parentUuid": "a549d62b_45271551",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "366429fa4de8734aac06963400efdf45b2207e1e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6af9c2fa_5f36b48f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1270601
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T18:02:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should implement CONFIG_PORT80_4_BYTE, which will change the port80 history buffer from uint16_t to uint32_t. We can then store the AMD 4 byte post codes naively, and even display them naively. This way we can see 0xEEE20400 when we type in `port80` into the console.",
      "parentUuid": "c7d34fa4_0791d80b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "366429fa4de8734aac06963400efdf45b2207e1e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
