    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c67430ae_31674f1a",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/lpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T02:52:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need to discuss this internally to get the answer.\nAlternatively, I assume that a platform will use either 1-byte or 4-byte at one time. How about add a config like \"CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_PORT80_4_BYTE\" so we can handle the grouping and re-order the endianness if needed when CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_PORT80_4_BYTE is defined?",
      "parentUuid": "ebf76514_b7949b57",
      "revId": "366429fa4de8734aac06963400efdf45b2207e1e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b505989e_4d31b77e",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/lpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T13:49:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to support both 1 byte and 4 byte port 80 codes at the same time. AMD PSP sends 4 byte codes while Coreboot sends 1 byte codes.",
      "parentUuid": "c67430ae_31674f1a",
      "revId": "366429fa4de8734aac06963400efdf45b2207e1e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d9d3872_b07467bc",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/lpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T08:39:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no straightforward way to know which bytes are sent together.\nAlternatively, we need to buffer the data in FIFO, analyze the offset filed at each byte to know if it should be grouped or not.\nThis is done in the patch set 3.",
      "parentUuid": "b505989e_4d31b77e",
